      "content_html": "<img src=\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=wildfiretoday.com&amp;sz=128\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\"/>\nBy Michael Hill For most of my career in the US federal government, I worked within a wildland fire organization that valued centralized leadership, standardized policy, and institutional accountability. Particularly within the US Forest Service’s aviation program, our operating procedures were not simply administrative requirements – they were the accumulated lessons of decades of experience, […]",
