      "content_html": "<img src=\"https://cdn.outsideonline.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/15791233676_5945a0cae9_o.jpg\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\"/>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 0.75em;padding:5px 10px;background:#f0f4f8;border-left:3px solid #7b9fc4;border-radius:3px;font-size:0.82em;color:#444;line-height:1.8;\">🎨 <a href=\"https://zirnhelt.github.io/super-rss-feed/review.html?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.outsideonline.com%2Fadventure-travel%2Fnational-parks%2Fhaunted-national-park-ghost-stories%2F\" style=\"color:#7b9fc4;text-decoration:none;\">✏️</a></p>\n<figure><img alt=\"The True Origins Behind America’s Most Famous National Park Ghost Stories\" src=\"https://cdn.outsideonline.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/15791233676_5945a0cae9_o.jpg?width=1200\"/></figure>\n<p>From totally made up hotel legends to real cave tragedies, here’s how fact and folklore created the most famous ghost stories in America's national parks.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.outsideonline.com/adventure-travel/national-parks/haunted-national-park-ghost-stories/\">The True Origins Behind America’s Most Famous National Park Ghost Stories</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.outsideonline.com\">Outside Online</a>.</p>",
